{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02210",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 4.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.2,
      "end_seconds": 20.29,
      "duration_seconds": 15.09,
      "text": "it's vomiting large amounts of fresh blood, mostly i kept putting it it off, which I know isn't sensible my neighbour said I should get it looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.03,
      "end_seconds": 27.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.9,
      "end_seconds": 39.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.51,
      "text": "Erm, hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.22,
      "end_seconds": 43.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.27,
      "end_seconds": 47.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "pretty mild, if I'm being honest"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.09,
      "end_seconds": 54.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "What about a swollen tummy, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.38,
      "end_seconds": 67.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.58,
      "text": "Yeah, um, I've had that since last night. As for swollen tummy, severe, really. Oh, and and being confused."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.47,
      "end_seconds": 75.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Have you had vomiting large amounts of fresh blood before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.61,
      "end_seconds": 82.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "oh, um, I had a similar thing last winter it went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.65,
      "end_seconds": 94.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "have you had any fever or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.6,
      "end_seconds": 98.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "No, no fever or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.45,
      "end_seconds": 103.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Okay, is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.98,
      "end_seconds": 107.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "No, uh, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.72,
      "end_seconds": 111.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.3,
      "end_seconds": 117.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.0,
      "end_seconds": 121.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.14,
      "end_seconds": 126.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.62,
      "end_seconds": 128.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.91,
      "end_seconds": 134.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.62,
      "end_seconds": 139.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "tell me about your eating"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.49,
      "end_seconds": 146.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.24,
      "end_seconds": 150.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.45,
      "end_seconds": 159.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "Um, you know, yes, I had a triple bypass, eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.9,
      "end_seconds": 164.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.01,
      "end_seconds": 167.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "I've got epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.11,
      "end_seconds": 169.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.81,
      "end_seconds": 178.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol, for nearly five years. I've got heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.67,
      "end_seconds": 181.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.81,
      "end_seconds": 190.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Yes, epilepsy is known to us, good to have that clear. Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.76,
      "end_seconds": 202.81,
      "duration_seconds": 11.05,
      "text": "Carbamazepine, 200 milligrams, twice a day for the seizures hmm, it's atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 204.59,
      "end_seconds": 209.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 10 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.49,
      "end_seconds": 213.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.77,
      "end_seconds": 227.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.25,
      "text": "Oh, I don't think I have it with me. I mean, it's metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day. I'm on alcohol every day, daily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.96,
      "end_seconds": 232.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.07,
      "end_seconds": 238.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 251.81,
      "end_seconds": 258.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier bP is 102 over 58, saturation 97 percent, pulse 97."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.9,
      "end_seconds": 267.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Okay, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.53,
      "end_seconds": 270.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.47,
      "end_seconds": 273.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.94,
      "end_seconds": 296.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "You are yellow, your tummy is swollen with fluid, and your pulse is very fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.71,
      "end_seconds": 302.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.51,
      "end_seconds": 332.83,
      "duration_seconds": 14.32,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I don't have a clear answer today: a bleed from enlarged veins in the gullet in liver disease is possible, and so is a bleeding ulcer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.56,
      "end_seconds": 338.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "So, um, do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.94,
      "end_seconds": 357.99,
      "duration_seconds": 19.05,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a bleed from enlarged veins in the gullet in liver disease do well once it's treated properly. Just to be sure I understood. You've had vomiting large amounts of fresh blood, mild, and no chest pain or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.58,
      "end_seconds": 359.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.67,
      "end_seconds": 365.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I'll request an urgent endoscopy, it'll help with variceal bleed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.4,
      "end_seconds": 370.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "So, where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.81,
      "end_seconds": 398.2,
      "duration_seconds": 26.39,
      "text": "Let's book urgent blood tests to look into major bleed. I'm gonna put you on terlipressin, 2 milligrams, now, single dose. It's for variceal bleeding. You are going straight to resus, I am starting two drips. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. The emergency team would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.73,
      "end_seconds": 403.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "I mean, sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.92,
      "end_seconds": 421.97,
      "duration_seconds": 17.05,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Book a review straight away. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.83,
      "end_seconds": 432.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "So, I take the terlipressin, 2 milligrams, now and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.99,
      "end_seconds": 439.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.6,
      "end_seconds": 444.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.44,
      "end_seconds": 446.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}